# ============================================================================
# 2026-07-14 comprehensive build-hygiene (source-provenance sweep, step 4 follow-on).
# The live v214 image was shipping ~23 dev/ops dirs, hundreds of *.bak files, a 14MB
# .jar, BifrostPortal.jsx, every Dockerfile, and deploy scripts into PRODUCTION.
# SAFE by construction: excludes ONLY provably-non-runtime content. Real source (*.py),
# runtime config (fleet_config.json, capability_registry.json, bifrost_shell_policy.json,
# executors.json, capability_profiles.json) and package dirs (backends/ sandbox/ skills/
# scripts/ tools/) are UNTOUCHED. The 130 excluded scratch .py were verified: none has a
# .pyc in the running pod AND none is imported by any kept source (grep-clean).
# NOTE: a pure `*`-floor whitelist is the ideal end-state -- deferred to the frozen
# rebuild where the minimal include-set can be smoke-tested (see handoff note).
# ============================================================================

# --- backups / superseded snapshots (never runtime) ---
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.pre-*bak
*.pre-*-bak
*.pre-training
*.pre-numctx-bak
*.pre-routervt-bak
*.broken-*
*.v72_backup
*_backup
*.block*.bak
decisions.md.bak-*

# 2026-09-04 (K-4). The patterns ABOVE match NOTHING. Measured against the running v410 image:
# 63 backup files shipped and zero were excluded, for three separate reasons --
#   42 files  `<name>.pre-<label>` (e.g. autopilot_graph.py.pre-v74). Every .pre- pattern above
#             requires a TRAILING "bak" (`*.pre-*bak`, `*.pre-*-bak`), and these do not have one.
#   18 files  live in a SUBDIRECTORY (backends/ollama.py.bak-...). In .dockerignore `*` does not
#             cross `/`, unlike .gitignore, so a bare `*.bak-*` is root-only. This is the cause
#             most likely to recur, because the pattern LOOKS right.
#    3 files  `.bak2`, `.bak3`, `.bak4` -- `*.bak` matches only exactly ".bak".
# Verified with excluded_from_image() from dirtycheck.py (the matcher that decides the build's
# -dirty stamp, 19 tests) over the full 363-file shipped list: catches 62 of 63, and newly
# excludes ZERO real files. The 63rd is under skills/, see the note at the end of this file.
**/*.bak*
**/*.pre-*
**/*.broken-*
**/*_backup

