# Re-assert the skills runtime registry include LAST (last-match-wins) so nothing above drops it.
!skills/
!skills/**

# 2026-08-03: keep the restored demo-bank harness tracked in git but OUT of the prod image.
scratchpad/

# 2026-09-03: three modules that COPY . . sweeps into the image although .gitignore already
# excludes them (lines 63, 72, 73) and NOTHING imports them -- verified 0 importers, no
# literal credentials. They fail the criterion .gitignore sets for itself: its 2026-08-12
# PROVENANCE FIX un-ignored four files BECAUSE main.py imports them at runtime. These are not
# imported by anything. Excluding them stops shipping code nothing runs and makes the image
# .py count match the git-tracked set, which is what the source_digest baseline records.
bifrost_telegram.py
format_stress_guard.py
tools/warmup.py

# 2026-09-04 (K-4), KNOWN AND LEFT ALONE: skills/router/SKILL.md.bak-ps1-20260519-200928 still
# ships. `!skills/**` above re-includes everything under skills/, and Docker is last-match-wins,
# so excluding it means putting `skills/**/*.bak*` AFTER that re-assertion -- deliberately
# breaking the invariant its own comment exists to protect ("re-assert LAST so nothing above
# drops it"). Risking the skills runtime registry falling out of a production image to remove
# one 4 KB stale file is not a good trade. Delete the file at source instead if it bothers you.

# ALSO CORRECTED 2026-09-04: __pycache__ is NOT shipped. The dirs visible in a running pod are
# written by Python at import time -- their mtimes are one second after container start, while
# real shipped source carries the build mtime. `__pycache__/` and `*.pyc` above are working
# correctly and need no change; an audit that counts files inside a RUNNING container is
# measuring the runtime, not the image.

# Protected-file ceremonies write <file>.ceremonyN-preimage-YYYYMMDD next to the
# file. Those match NONE of the backup patterns above (*.bak, *_backup, **/*.bak*),
# so before 2026-09-22 every one of them reached the build context and made the
# build -dirty -- an image matching NO commit. Caught by dirtycheck.py on v454;
# the tempting wrong answer there is -Force, which ships exactly that image.
*-preimage-*

# ---- added for the never-block floor ----
# harness/router/ is a context ROOT for the four Dockerfiles beside this file, so
# this ignore file is live even though nothing in deploy/compose.yaml builds here.
# It carried none of the credential floor; it does now.

# ---- never, under any circumstances ----
# Every pattern below is the floor in deploy/images/NEVER-BLOCK-SHAPES.txt, carried
# verbatim. The floor is a MINIMUM: a never-block may deny more. Do not reflow or
# re-order these lines -- tools/check_never_block_shapes.py compares them as text.

# --- environment and secrets ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/secrets/
**/.secrets/
**/*.secret
**/*.secrets
**/credentials.json
**/*credential*
**/*-credentials*
**/auth.json
**/.sops.yaml
**/.sops/
**/*.kubeconfig
**/kubeconfig
**/kubeconfig.*

# --- keys and certificates ---
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/id_rsa
**/id_rsa.*
**/id_ed25519
**/id_ed25519.*
**/*.ppk
**/known_hosts

# --- tokens ---
**/*.token
**/.netrc
**/_netrc
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc

# --- repository metadata, which carries remotes and credentials of its own ---
**/.git-credentials
**/.git/
**/.github/
